  "notes": "Drawn from N965AV (2026-01-24, left side; N762AV the same day agrees) and HK-5366 (2025-02-22, from below: belly, engines, winglets); the fin's facets read from N967AV (2024). The swoosh's lower edge, near y -0.8, is judged from level side views: no view from below of an aircraft with the swoosh was found, so whether it wraps under the belly is unknown. The tiny type designation ('A320neo') by the cockpit is left out. The right side wasn't checked. Many aircraft still carry the 2013 capitalised 'Avianca' titles (standard-2013). The 787s wear the same layout. Ex-Viva Air A320neos (e.g. HK-5366, seen 2025) were repainted more simply: the same titles, bird, fin and engines but no swoosh on the aft fuselage. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on N965AV, placed by its doors: the title runs 0.229 to 0.412 (lowercase 0.75 of the cap height, type.xHeight); the swoosh agrees within about 0.3 m and its edges are curves, now drawn smooth. drawnOn A320: the A320neo (the commonest type) has the A320's fuselage.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximation (an all-red body). The October 2023 rebrand lowercased the wordmark; the rest of the 2013 scheme (standard-2013), which replaced the cream-and-red scheme, stayed."
}
